<UserControl x:Class="Accel.App.Controls.EffortBarsControl"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             SnapsToDevicePixels="True">
    <!--
        P1-T4 (revised): a single radial ring gauge next to the model badge - Level (0-4, see
        EffortBarLevel.Resolve) fills TrackRing's outline clockwise from the top, one quarter-turn
        per level (low=1/4, medium=1/2, high=3/4). Max (4/4) renders as a solid filled disc instead
        of a full ring - a 360-degree arc is a degenerate WPF ArcSegment (start and end coincide),
        and a solid disc is also a stronger, shape-distinct "fully committed" signal rather than
        just "a ring that happens to be complete". Level 0 (unknown) shows only the hollow track,
        same "visibly different from no control at all" rule the old bars used.

        FillArc's geometry is entirely code-behind (EffortBarsControl.xaml.cs.ApplyLevel) since the
        arc's end point/large-arc-flag depend on Level; TrackRing here is the one part that never
        changes, so it stays as plain XAML.
    -->
    <Grid Width="14" Height="14" VerticalAlignment="Bottom">
        <Ellipse x:Name="TrackRing" Width="12" Height="12" StrokeThickness="2" Fill="Transparent" />
        <Path x:Name="FillArc" Width="14" Height="14" StrokeThickness="2"
              StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" />
        <Ellipse x:Name="FillDisc" Width="12" Height="12" Visibility="Collapsed" />
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
